          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 55,
              "body": "```suggestion\nThese use cases also extend into the legal realm. An enterprise using an AI agent for screening job applicants may later get sued by an applicant that was passed up for a role. The enterprise might subpoena the AI agent vendor, requesting a full trace of what the AI Agent did, and why. Similarly, a governmental body investigating malicious steps taken by an AI Agent, might request a full log of all of the sessions that AI Agent had.\n```",
              "createdAt": "2026-10-30T11:39:14Z",
              "updatedAt": "2026-10-30T11:39:15Z"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOVYb3qc8AAAABVHJ93Q",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "77b7388"
          },
          "author": "henkbirkholz",
          "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
          "state": "APPROVED",
          "body": "I like the additional goals (and editorial on goal representation). The abstract now covers a small ref to VACR, which I like a lot (better than the clumsy references in the body). The introduction might require some more massaging, but with your proposed changes is good as is!\n\nI'll follow up with an editorial pass of \"on sentence per linebreak\" for easier to read diffs.",
